-- title:
--   A favoured cone slice fills at least a $1/L$ fraction of its cube
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a configuration (cone field) on $\mathbb{R}^d$ and let $F$ be a *reference family*
--   of aperture $\theta$ for it (Lean: `F : RefFamily Γ θ`): a finite set $F.\mathrm{axes}$ of axes,
--   each carrying a reference cone $V = F.\mathrm{cone}(v)$ of aperture $\theta$, such that the family
--   covers $\Gamma$ pointwise. Write $L := |F.\mathrm{axes}|$ for the number of reference cones. For a
--   mesh $h$, a point $u$ and a reference cone $V$, let
--
--   $$A_h^{V}(u) \;:=\; \texttt{cubeCone } \Gamma\ V\ h\ u \;=\; \{\,x \in A_h(u) \;:\; V \subseteq \Gamma(x)\,\}$$
--
--   be the slice of the cube $A_h(u) := \texttt{cube } h\ u$ consisting of the points whose own cone
--   contains $V$. Say that the axis $v$ is *$h$-favoured by majority at $u$* (Lean:
--   `IsFavoured F h u v`) when $v \in F.\mathrm{axes}$ **and** the slice $A_h^{F.\mathrm{cone}(v)}(u)$ has maximal
--   Lebesgue measure among the slices coming from the reference cones of $F$.
--
--   If $v$ is $h$-favoured by majority at $u$, then
--
--   $$\lambda_d\big(A_h(u)\big) \;\le\; L \cdot \lambda_d\big(A_h^{F.\mathrm{cone}(v)}(u)\big).$$
--
--   This is the pigeonhole step behind the "favoured by majority" device: the $L$ slices cover the
--   cube, so the largest of them carries at least a $1/L$ fraction of its volume. It is what converts a
--   statement about the cone at a *typical* point of a cube into a statement about one fixed reference
--   cone attached to the whole cube, with a loss of only the fixed factor $L$, independent of $h$ and
--   $u$.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** No positivity hypothesis is placed on the mesh $h$; for degenerate $h$ both
--   sides vanish and the inequality is trivial. The cardinality $L$ is that of a `Finset` of axes, so it
--   is finite by construction, and both volumes are elements of `ℝ≥0∞`.
